<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">São Luís</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">São Luís is a port city on the island of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maranhao">Maranhão</a> in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a>. It was founded in 1612 by the French as Fort Saint-Louis, centre of Equinoctial <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, and taken by the Portuguese in 1615. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> held it from 1641 to 1644. It was the capital of the State of Maranhão and, after the capital moved to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belem">Belém</a>, of the later State of Maranhão and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piaui">Piauí</a>. Its colonial centre is a World Heritage Site.</p></div>
